  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Emerald Mountain was originally developed in the 1970s as a planned community designed to blend residential living with natural landscapes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/alabama_emerald-mountain"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community’s name comes from its lush, green hills, and the Emerald Mountain Nature Preserve offers hiking trails and scenic views.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/alabama_emerald-mountain"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Emerald Mountain’s homeowners association is mandatory, and an architectural review board oversees design to maintain the area’s cohesive aesthetic.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emerald_Mountain%2C_Alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The subdivision includes a golf club, a tennis center, and an equestrian center, making it a hub for outdoor recreation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emerald_Mountain%2C_Alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Emerald Mountain’s development features ranch‑style homes from the 1990s and newer New Traditional dwellings built through the 2020s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.homes.com/local-guide/emerald-mountain-al/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The community sits beside a river, with much of its terrain wooded and hilly, offering a picturesque setting for residents.",
